Abstract
We provide a formal mathematical specification of the Twin Prime Sieve framework, consisting of the Sieve Integer sequence SI, the Twin Prime Pair map TPP, and the Twin Prime Search function TPS. We prove the bijection theorem, the Modular Resonance Theorem, the Gap Divisibility Corollary, and the computational equivalence of the TP-SI Interval Conjecture with the Twin Prime Conjecture (TPC). All results are computationally verified to 10,000.

